# Read by Vite, which looks for `.env` beside its own `vite.config.ts` and nowhere
# else — which is why this is a second file rather than more lines in the root
# `.env.example` that Python reads. Copy it to `frontend/.env`, which the root
# `.gitignore`'s `.env` rule already covers at any depth.
#
# One value belongs here, and it is the only one of the issuer's three that is not a
# secret: the publishable key, which the dashboard itself describes as safe to share.
# The secret key and the PEM are read by the API and live in the root `.env` — a
# secret in this file would be compiled into the bundle and served to every visitor.
#
# **It is inlined at build time.** Vite substitutes the literal into the bundle, so
# setting this on a server after a deploy does nothing: a console with no sign-in is
# a console that was built without it.
#
# Declaring nothing here is declaring no issuer, and the console then renders every
# screen and attends no door — the reading `console/door.ts` states and
# `api/http.ts` sends: no `Authorization` header at all. That is not an open bench.
# The gate is the API's, which refuses to boot with no issuer of its own and refuses
# every headerless request when it has one; what this buys is that a clone with no
# account still runs, and that `npm run e2e` needs none.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
